{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483086-which-spatbooks-would-you-not-crossover","id":1483086,"title":"Which spatbooks would you NOT crossover","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-04T17:21:22-07:00","id":1483086,"title":"Which spatbooks would you NOT crossover","content":"A while back I got the Chronicles of Darkness book and the big three spalt books from DTRPG. Last night, I went on a wee spending spree and got Promethean, Changeling, Mummy, and Gheist.<br /> <br /> I have this weird idea that's been percolating in my head for a chronicle where a coterie (or maybe just several solitary vampires) move to a small, unremarkable city in the hope of finding uncontested territory to claim a domain. Upon arrival, they find out not only have at least two vampires got their first but so have Mages investigating local landmarks, a gang of Pure Werewolves, a small court of Changelings, and the occasional Spirit that's running loose.<br /> <br /> Before I take this idea further, I wonder what NOT to use. Prometheans seem difficult, as I get the impression they're supposed to keep moving (although the flavor text for the Ordo Dracul describes an encounter with what reads like a Frankenstein to me). Hunters, I don't know what to do with them besides, well, hunting. Mummies seem cool, except I'm worried they might seem TOO cool and the players may want to stop playing Vampires.<br /> <br /> Are there any Monsters that you think should just NOT have crossovers? You can say Vampires if you want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 06-13-2022, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T18:24:59-07:00","id":1483089,"title":"","content":"Like, on principle? None.<br /> <br /> There are some that are harder to work around in contexts than others, but often those experiences are more flexible than they might anticipate. Of the 11, I imagine.....Vampire, Promethean, Hunter, and Mummy are the ones you have to apply some thought to. <br /> <br /> Vampire's big thing is primarily the night restrictions and their lack of larger scope access that some of the other splats, but there's actually a lot of tools for skirting around and flirting with daytime operation (often with penalties and struggles, but it's not an absolute closed door), and most monsters are still more inclined and rewarded for night operation anyways, and vampires carry a lot of direct effectiveness for their sphere that helps them keep up for some of that larger scope problem.<br /> <br /> Prometheans may be focused on their Pilgrimage, but the way to Dawn has many roads, and even scenarios completely unrooted in humanity are useful for contrast if a Promethean is willing to reflect and learn on it in such a way. More often, though, there's very rarely an experience that doesn't engage with humanity and reflect on it in some way that yields the spiritual calculus and vitriol that helps them on their way. More importantly is Disquiet and Wasteland management, but that's gonna be true no matter what, and it is IS a thing that can be managed.<br /> <br /> The conflict for Hunters is that in any situation where it's a human life versus a monstrous one and the hunter prioritizes the latter over the former, it's psychologically very hard for them. Beyond that though, Hunter do a lot of things in addition to hunting-those in Compacts and Conspiracies have more direct....directives, but just about any hunter can benefit from learning more about the supernatural community and how it's various subsections work together (or against each other), shoring up resources both mundane and supernatural for defense and comfort (and okay, for murderkilling), and just learning or experiencing new things. I had a Hunter campaign that could be more adequately called monster ambassador-ing, and while some ardent killjoys are nothing but death to anything resembling monsters, more have fraught but workable relationships to monsters who aren't being their worst selves all the time.<br /> <br /> Mummies, by and large, seem the most restricted, since there are penalties for not being focused on their First and Final Purposes-but it's not the <i>most</i> hyper strict thing ever. The Arisen have room to go and explore and do other things do long as it doesn't completely derail their attention, and the time they could spend learning to appreciate trap music, experiment with food dishes, and/or pursuing Memory (and other like) can easily go into crossover game stuff. It's made all the easier if that crossover game stuff IS their First Purpose, ala everyone else being in their cult, or at least successfully petitioning the cult to call the Arisen to their aid., but even if not, so long as the Purposes are intertwined into the narrative (even antagonistically), it's fine. The only other concern is their power at the start, and that just requires smart planning-if they can do it in The Hobbit and Avengers Endgame, you can keep a Sekhem 10 Arisen player busy and happy while everyone else is playing scrambling hatchlings under their necrotic wings. <br /> <br /> Most crossover concerns come down to creatively employing and utilizing the pieces that keep things fun.<br /> ----<br /> <br /> Now, <i>should you</i> include these, or any other ones? Honestly, it comes down to management and usable material. Sure, it can be cool to make it clear that your metropolitan area is dense and busy with the supernatural (comparatively), but are you really gonna incorporate <i>every single splat </i>into the story hooks and over all projected path of the game going forward? Probably not. It comes down to what's going to keep the gameplay a tight and fun experience.<br /> <br /> In this case, a Vampire game contesting against the presence of pack of werewolves, a cabal of mages, the assumed corresponding impact and influence of spirits and the Shadow along with those two, and a whole court of changelings (and it's correlated assumed impact and influence of hobgoblins and the Hedge)-all of that makes for a pretty tight and dynamic landscape to game in on it's own, if it's within the scope people are going for. You don't want to load up your plate with <i>too much</i> to deal with, and even in settings where everyone is populous, present, and active and it'd be weird if they weren't, it's important to keep in mind that the game takes place in a corner of the world, and not <i>everything</i> is going to have something to do with that corner. Keep only that which matters to the big picture of your chronicle, if it turns out to be too lean, then you can add in something from another gameline that plays well with the conflicts and themes of that game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T09:09:13-07:00","id":1483223,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't at all? None. <br /> <br /> But that said I can understand why some are more difficult. Mummies with how they start at max power and fall could be hard to work with but you might find a way. Especially as there are ways to slow the fall so maybe you can have them in the middle of a decent and holding their current state or regaining power. But that might be difficult and different to a standard game of mummy. In a similar way mage can be a struggle because of the flexibility and power of their arcana. <br /> <br /> Largely, you just have to understand that the gamelines are internally balanced and not truly cross balanced. Your group has to be willing to work together and make the mix work and focus on the group more so than the individual, more than a normal game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T10:36:29-07:00","id":1483229,"title":"","content":"I agree with ArcaneArts on this. The NWoD/CoD/GMC rules are a <i>lot</i> more compatible with crossovers than O/CWoD based on what I\u2019ve heard, so it\u2019s ultimately up to a combination of what sort of setting you\u2019re trying to make, what sort of game you\u2019re wanting to run, what you and your players would genuinely consider fun, and your own preferences.<br /> <br /> Though one possible work around could be that, while the various splats do indeed <i>exist</i> in your setting, none beyond those you\u2019ve listed as already being present have yet found a reason to actually head towards the city. Heck, you could even try mixing in the big four \u2018fan-splats\u2019 if you so chose!<br /> <br /> What I\u2019m getting at is that <i><b><u>all</u></b></i> of the official, \u2018canon\u2019 splats can easily be used, or not used, in a game setting if you can pull it off. It simply depends on what sort of story that you, the storyteller, wish to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T11:17:46-07:00","id":1483237,"title":"","content":"I don't recommend mixed splats for the PCs. That said, all other games can definitely be used as source books for the game you're running. Having the PCs accidentally disturb the tomb of a mummy or cross paths with a promethean who wishes to learn from them could work great in basically any game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T08:14:13-07:00","id":1483376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483086-which-spatbooks-would-you-not-crossover?p=1483237#post1483237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recommend mixed splats for the PCs. That said, all other games can definitely be used as source books for the game you're running. Having the PCs accidentally disturb the tomb of a mummy or cross paths with a promethean who wishes to learn from them could work great in basically any game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I have something to say regarding mixed-splat troupes.<br /> <br /> Namely, while it <i>can</i> be really hard to pull off, it\u2019s still possible. One just has to develop some sort of in-universe justification as to just <i>why</i> all these different supernaturals are working together, instead of just leaving or tearing each other apart, and maybe also play off of the drama spawned by the meeting and interactions of differing world views and belief systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T10:08:28-07:00","id":1483383,"title":"","content":"CoD makes crossovers relatively easy, the two games I would be the most worried about are purely for meta reasons and I think that it is nothing in the world that makes them bad, but just the mechanics of the splats that hinder them a bit.<br /> <br /> 1. Mages, considering you need almost an active excel sheet to cast magic and how cumbersome the casting system itself is, along with all of the myriads of systems that has to be kept in mind with Mage. Mage Sight is an all-encompassing system by itself, and the math needed for the spells, and similar. That is before you even get into the discussion of Arcana vs the other powers which I frankly don't find that interesting, but Mage is a game that if you start with more experienced characters can lead to one character eclipsing the rest.<br /> <br /> 2. Mummy...and that is simply due to the focused nature of mummies and their very powerful starting point. But I think you can handle this with good STing, compared to Mage where I honestly see the idea of having a mage with the rest as a bit nightmarish. &quot;Okay I am going to cast a fireball!&quot; *sits down to begin calculating yantras and the spell factors...15 minutes later the fireball is good to go*. Mummy just has a lot of power to deal with and their Judges yelling at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T10:11:14-07:00","id":1483384,"title":"","content":"The bigger issue of crossover troupes is that it's generally not as satisfying if you haven't had the experience of splats in isolation, or as originally intended. It's a similar sort of problem to playing in a shard or Dark Era or with major rule changes like you'd find in the Chronicler's Guides*. All of these things are there to deliver a deviation from the norm, that makes a character's experience as a splat <i>that much more</i> abnormal, weird, unique, and challenging-an appreciation that's hard to have if you've never experienced all the weird, unique, and challenging aspects that form the fog of &quot;normal&quot; experience for any given splat.<br /> <br /> That said, there's nothing wrong with doing a mixed troupe outside of personal preferences in how themes and ideas are handled in regards to it, and in fact it was a built in feature from the word go. It's just more rewarding for more experienced players than for newbies, a nuanced and different tapestry for the former where it's otherwise just D&amp;D for the latter.<br /> <br /> *or, hell, even Beast: the Primordial in a non-crossover capacity, to a certain degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T12:34:49-07:00","id":1483393,"title":"","content":"Depends a lot on what you want to do with them. Like, the last game I ran had the mage PCs making friends with a vampire, and getting to know some of the local domain. Still, I didn't bother that much with being strictly accurate with how Requiem mechanics work. The friendly NPC could move around so quickly that they seemed to teleport, but I didn't really care how many dots in Celerity she had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T12:38:54-07:00","id":1483394,"title":"","content":"Mages don't play well with other splats for purely mechanical reasons, mummies are a close second but the others can reasonably play together in a Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T14:39:13-07:00","id":1483401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483086-which-spatbooks-would-you-not-crossover?p=1483394#post1483394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages don't play well with other splats for purely mechanical reasons, mummies are a close second but the others can reasonably play together in a Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage's mechanical reasons come from that, in a long enough run from the beginning, they have a large amount of variety of action that is honestly going to be decently matched by the much more rapid progression of their peers. It's more openly intimidating, and sure a Storyteller benefits from running a Mage game first, but it's not actually all that challenging even if you just start by understanding the art of alternating spotlights and providing opposition that has it's pieces work in tandem with each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T14:49:12-07:00","id":1483403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483086-which-spatbooks-would-you-not-crossover?p=1483401#post1483401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage's mechanical reasons come from that, in a long enough run from the beginning, they have a large amount of variety of action that is honestly going to be decently matched by the much more rapid progression of their peers. It's more openly intimidating, and sure a Storyteller benefits from running a Mage game first, but it's not actually all that challenging even if you just start by understanding the art of alternating spotlights and providing opposition that has it's pieces work in tandem with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By their peers you mean the other splats? Because mages are very quick in getting xp compared to many splats (vampires particularly), I am running a geist chronicle with a mage player and I'm seriously considering killing it, mage is possibly the hardest game to run and if you add them in a multisplat, it becomes borderline impossible without either you nerfing mages or the mage players holding back with their spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T15:19:07-07:00","id":1483404,"title":"","content":"A crossover game I have been wanting to run for a while now is a short chronicle focused on a group of childhood friends all grown up who have not seen each other in at least 5 years [the players]. They all come back to their hometown for a [reunion/festival/funeral/murder mystery/all of the above] and generally catch up on each others' lives. Of course, each has been turned into a different kind of monster since last meeting, and everyone assumes everyone else is still a normal mortal. Comedy ensues.<br /> <br /> I guess what I am saying is, when it comes to crossovers...<br /> Embrace chaos.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T15:23:56-07:00","id":1483405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483086-which-spatbooks-would-you-not-crossover?p=1483383#post1483383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CoD makes crossovers relatively easy, the two games I would be the most worried about are purely for meta reasons and I think that it is nothing in the world that makes them bad, but just the mechanics of the splats that hinder them a bit.<br /> <br /> 1. Mages, considering you need almost an active excel sheet to cast magic and how cumbersome the casting system itself is, along with all of the myriads of systems that has to be kept in mind with Mage. Mage Sight is an all-encompassing system by itself, and the math needed for the spells, and similar. That is before you even get into the discussion of Arcana vs the other powers which I frankly don't find that interesting, but Mage is a game that if you start with more experienced characters can lead to one character eclipsing the rest.<br /> <br /> 2. Mummy...and that is simply due to the focused nature of mummies and their very powerful starting point. But I think you can handle this with good STing, compared to Mage where I honestly see the idea of having a mage with the rest as a bit nightmarish. &amp;quot;Okay I am going to cast a fireball!&amp;quot; *sits down to begin calculating yantras and the spell factors...15 minutes later the fireball is good to go*. Mummy just has a lot of power to deal with and their Judges yelling at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This why I pre write my standard way of casting spells that my character regularly uses. Then it's just a quick alteration of one or more spell factors if needed but far less work than doing from square 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T15:41:34-07:00","id":1483409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483086-which-spatbooks-would-you-not-crossover?p=1483403#post1483403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> By their peers you mean the other splats? Because mages are very quick in getting xp compared to many splats (vampires particularly), I am running a geist chronicle with a mage player and I'm seriously considering killing it, mage is possibly the hardest game to run and if you add them in a multisplat, it becomes borderline impossible without either you nerfing mages or the mage players holding back with their spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying this as gently as I can-having read about your problems in the Geist Answers thread, I'm disinclined to believe that this experience is rooted in a problem of clashing mechanics. Yes, Mages are versatile, and yes, Arcane Beats provides some decent acceleration, but decent planning can account for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T15:49:28-07:00","id":1483412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483086-which-spatbooks-would-you-not-crossover?p=1483409#post1483409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying this as gently as I can-having read about your problems in the Geist Answers thread, I'm disinclined to believe that this experience is rooted in a problem of clashing mechanics. Yes, Mages are versatile, and yes, Arcane Beats provides some decent acceleration, but decent planning can account for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I already wrote in the geist tread that I'm not good enough to run a mage game so you can say that, I don't have any problem in admitting my limitations but I will tell you that pretty much all the mage STs I asked for suggestions (many of whom had run mage since 1st ed) told me to spare me the trouble and ban them from the game, maybe you are better at storytelling then all of them but I quite frankly don't know how you are going to plan for reality warpers that can do anything they want, it's already difficult to juggle together different splats and putting mage in it (which is the most difficult game of the CoD line) make everything even more difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T16:36:49-07:00","id":1483418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483086-which-spatbooks-would-you-not-crossover?p=1483376#post1483376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have something to say regarding mixed-splat troupes.<br /> <br /> Namely, while it <i>can</i> be really hard to pull off, it\u2019s still possible. One just has to develop some sort of in-universe justification as to just <i>why</i> all these different supernaturals are working together, instead of just leaving or tearing each other apart, and maybe also play off of the drama spawned by the meeting and interactions of differing world views and belief systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't the difficulty of running a mixed game (although it certainly is more difficult than a single splat game). The problem is the fact that each game has specific themes and gameplay loops that are generally carefully crafted by the devs and writers. The various different CofD games are <i>different games</i>, and trying to play multiple different games at the same time means you need to axe a lot of the themes and foci of those games. You can't get around that, and that's why I never recommend mixed splat groups.<br /> <br /> That said, if you've figured out some shared themes to base your game on (like a paranoid and violent vampire/werewolf game where you're forced to cooperate to stop the Strix from hunting down and possessing your Touchstones/pack members) and experienced enough to pull it off, or just don't give a shit about such things because you just want to play some monsters, then you can absolutely have a great time playing a mixed splat group.<br /> But I'd still recommend playing as either vampires or werewolves in such a game. I'm leaning more towards werewolves, with the vampires as NPCs being just the right mix of helpful and untrustworthy to put the players on edge each time they're forced to work with them. The contrast between Strix and spirits (or hosts) also make werewolves more interesting to me in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T16:42:34-07:00","id":1483419,"title":"","content":"The problem is I want to run a Vampire Chronicle, with Vampire players, just with the potential to run into other creatures. Like a bar or store might serve as a Changeling Court. Or one of the highways out of town might be Werewolf turf. And the local university would be claimed by someone local Vampires think is a mage, but the local Magi think must be a Vampire.<br /> <br /> I want Vampire PCs, I just don't want them neatly walled off from (most of) the other freaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T18:56:12-07:00","id":1483432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483086-which-spatbooks-would-you-not-crossover?p=1483419#post1483419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Vampire PCs, I just don't want them neatly walled off from (most of) the other freaks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the games already do that. There aren't neat walls between the splats, they're just uncommon enough and clustered that it is plausible that there won't be enough of them in any given city to make a local society if you don't need there to be, and perfectly reasonable secrecy and paranoia (coupled, in some cases, with being born and raised a mortal with Health, Willpower, and Integrity to worry about) means most of them hear strange rumors and leave well enough alone if they don't have a stake in investigating.<br /> <br /> That store serves as a front for one court in a freehold? Fine, dandy, that's maybe thirty people if the roads to Faerie are well-traveled in town, and if you don't wanna deal with them you can find a different place to shop or keep an ear out for who to avoid.<br /> <br /> That stretch of highway has a pack dealing with litterbugs? Don't litter or else find a different road out of town, and if you're interested in collaborating you know where to find them.<br /> <br /> Some weird witch-thing is hunkered down in the uni? Unless you want a piece of what it's got you can ignore it as long as you don't have business in the stacks, and if you've got an interest in it you probably know a guy (or a guy who knows a guy) who has a better idea of what's up.<br /> <br /> Like, part of the reason I'm currently consuming the line that I am is because one of the local changeling courts in my game is heavily involved with a demonic Agency tangled up in the history of the city going back to the nineteenth century. Most of the court only knows that they're working with an old secret society that serves a weird fallen angel whose Bargain wards off the Fae in exchange for keeping the power grid and the storm drains running their weird occult safeguards. If they put it out there that some of the cultists and courtiers they've been working with are other demons (as some of them suspect and leadership knows) it would change the context of their relationship in a way none of that guilt-ridden assemblage is ready to deal with, so all sides keep things professional.<br /> <br /> If you're going to be running a game where the main draw is &quot;vampires trying to carve out territory in an unfamiliar city with lots of different weird shit in small numbers already claiming the good spots,&quot; access to the local rumor mill is going to be a disincentive to go for places that seem occupied unless the prize is very tempting and the players are already secure enough to start going after other folks' squatting rights. Without that kind of forewarning, it's very easy to see the format devolving into &quot;stumble into contested ground, sleep suboptimally if you manage to win the fight and moreso if you lose.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, this does seem like the kind of game for which a Beast NPC or two would be worthwhile to have, both as a source of information on local monsters and as a fallback source of shelter if sleeping rough looks to be the only option; even without the book, if you know that a character can identity unveiled monsters at a glance, turn select locations into entrances to a monstrous stronghold, sustain itself on making sure you're well-fed, and be very persuasive to monsters who haven't decided they're a bastard yet (and very differently persuasive to ones who have), you can get a lot of use out of that lady who turned into a simurgh for half a second when she clawed that drunkard's arm with more force than sharp fingernails could justify or that enby who made a tourist dissolve into a screaming fit by remarking that it looked like it was going to rain.<br /> <br /> On a different angle, if there's mages around, they're looking into local Mysteries, of which the other monsters constitute at least as many as there are other monsters; depending on their morals, they may also serve as a useful source of information, albeit maybe not as broad a variety without bringing in the resources of a Caucus from further afield, in exchange for whatever the PCs can offer them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T21:58:27-07:00","id":1483441,"title":"","content":"On record, because it hasn't been said yet: a coterie of vampires carving out a space of their own against werewolves, mages, and changelings sounds really cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T13:35:06-07:00","id":1487051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1483086-which-spatbooks-would-you-not-crossover?p=1483419#post1483419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is I want to run a Vampire Chronicle, with Vampire players, just with the potential to run into other creatures. Like a bar or store might serve as a Changeling Court. Or one of the highways out of town might be Werewolf turf. And the local university would be claimed by someone local Vampires think is a mage, but the local Magi think must be a Vampire.<br /> <br /> I want Vampire PCs, I just don't want them neatly walled off from (most of) the other freaks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding Arcane here, that does sound awesome!<br /> <br /> Also, and I am probably alone in this, but to me, this is not really crossover-play - having all Vampire-PCs means things are pretty balanced as far as the interparty's versatility and powers are concerned, and the focus and purity of the themes of a Vampire game can be upheld to pretty much <i>whichever point you desire</i>. <br /> Sure, a Mage PC that's crafty (don't let Chemists take Matter as an Arcana) can derail everything, but if it's Mage NPCs, I don't think you need to worry too much. You don't have to bother with the Mage's versatility overshadowing the rest, or the Werewolf designated-smart-guy casually stealing the fighting spotlight thanks do Basu-Im. These are NPCs. They do what you want them to. Unlike players =D<br /> <br /> <br /> And remember: You are not bound to represent the other Splats 100%. Your goal is a fun experience and telling a Chronicle with your players. As Michael stated:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Depends a lot on what you want to do with them. Like, the last game I ran had the mage PCs making friends with a vampire, and getting to know some of the local domain. Still, I didn't bother that much with being strictly accurate with how Requiem mechanics work. The friendly NPC could move around so quickly that they seemed to teleport, but I didn't really care how many dots in Celerity she had. </div> </div> </div>If things don't fit the story you want to tell, change them. The exact calculations for a mage fireball are too cumbersome? Simplify it to a usable level that still makes sense. A Werewolf's abilities should render his problem moot? Do the ST thing and come up with why exactly he cannot use them. You need Changeling's Mien to work differently? Go ahead and change it up.<br /> Unless you create a full NPCsheet for every character beforehand according to creation rules, this should come naturally. <br /> This gets easier the less the others know about the other splats, though. However, if it catches them off-guard: how dare they apply meta-knowledge!? xD<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}